Fenrir, a newly trained priestess of Mercury ventured into the
Dungeons of Doom with hopes of retrieving the fabled Amulet of Yendor
from the depths of Gehennom.

This was a fabulously generous game: she found a shield of reflection
and speed boots lying around dungeon level three, ran into team ant
(and nearly YASD'ed!), did Sokoban and got the BoH, then found a bones
file of an Archeologist with two magic markers and a GDSM.

Did the Quest by taming all the purple worms and minotaurs Nalzok
summoned and easily obtained the silver bell and the Mitre of
Holiness. Beat Medusa, stormed the castle and wished for more magic
markers and an "oMB.

Enchanted all stuff to +4, +5 and got Grayswandir as a sacrifice gift,
with armor class -37 descended into Gehennom. Asmodeus and Baalzebub
didn't know what struck them, Orcus gave a lot of trouble, summoned
Yeenoghu (but no Demogorgon) and had a wand of digging.

Marked the vibrating square, then the purple worm ate Vlad. Ran into
an arch-lich. Fought two master liches. Genocided all L.

Fenrir woke the wizard with a death ray, but killed him over the moat
and had run out of wands of cold. She had to drop everything at a
side, put on her "oMB, and dive into the moat to get the book.
Levelported somewhere near the vibrating square, went to the sanctuary
and killed the high priest of Moloch.

y - The Amulet of Yendor named real one, WHAMMO!

The misterious force was merciless-- she had to run around the 45th
floor about fifteen times.

There was a scary moment when she foolishly took off her shield of
reflection to see what happened if you tamed a purple worm that was
engulfing you, and sure enough, a blue D from the other side of the
level hit her with a lightning blast.

Her =oC, =oFA, =oL, and her /oD went BLAM! Fenrir had to use her last
wish for free action and had to resolute to polypilling to get the
